### CHANGELOG.md
# Changelog

## 1.0.0
- Built the Brightlane Commerce Engineering theme with responsive templates, header panels, forms, newsletter management, local assets, and compiled production bundles.


### docs/getting-started.md
# Getting Started

Install the theme in WordPress, activate it, then create pages for Home, About, Services, Work, Blog, Contact, and Policy content. Assign the homepage to use `front-page.php`, apply the included page templates where appropriate, and configure Primary and Footer menus.

Run `npm install` when dependencies are not present, then use `npm run build` to regenerate `assets/css/bundle.css` and `assets/js/bundle.js`.


### docs/customization.md
# Customization

Customize global colors, spacing, typography, and component styling in `src/scss/`. The compiled files in `assets/css/bundle.css` and `assets/js/bundle.js` are generated outputs and should keep their required names.

Business copy lives in templates and helper data arrays. Replace neutral Brightlane Commerce Engineering content with verified business details only when those details are supplied.


### assets/icons/README.md
# Icons

`icon1.svg` is the local Brightlane Commerce Engineering compass-star mark used in the header, mobile drawer, and footer. Store only sanitized SVG interface icons in this folder and reference them through WordPress theme-path functions. Keep third-party logo marks and remote icon packs out of this folder.


### blocks/README.md
# Blocks

This theme does not ship custom block registrations. The folder is reserved for future block documentation and should stay separate from template parts, page templates, and compiled assets.


### accessibility/README.md
# Accessibility

Brightlane Commerce Engineering includes visible focus states, semantic landmarks, keyboard-operable menu panels, mobile accordions, accessible filtering controls, and server-side validation for public forms. Closed dropdowns, drawers, accordions, and filter results use `hidden` so inactive controls are not left in the keyboard order.

Motion is restrained and disabled where users request reduced motion. Color is paired with text, labels, or state changes for validation and filtering feedback.


### LICENSE.txt
License

This generated WordPress theme is provided for use within the Nolan Young Theme Factory workflow. Third-party assets, if added later, must retain their own documented license terms.


